/*****************************************************************************
    nameRecurse -- SEQ 31 step 0. TWO questions, one run, both GREEN (exit 0).

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    Q1. DOES A NAMED SELF-CALL TRIP THE `recursive` INFERENCE?  -> YES.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    The one thing source cannot answer. saveLocalFields/restoreLocalFields are
    readable (GroupActions.rtn:687/516) and so is runAction's
    `if field.recursive` gate (:570/572) -- what is NOT readable is whether a
    bare named self-call sets `recursive`, because the inference is a syntactic
    identity check against currentMETHOD (ruleActions.rtn) and `this(...)`
    demonstrably does NOT trip it (corpus CLAIM KANT-7).

    `probe` assigns a scalar local, recurses BY NAME, then reads its own local
    AFTER the call -- the read genEmit's note 2 forbids under `this()`.

        PER-FRAME (recursive IS set):  each AFTER reads its OWN frame's mark.
        SHARED    (NOT set):           every AFTER reads L-deep, the innermost.

    MEASURED: ENTER outer/inner/deep then AFTER deep/inner/outer, each AFTER
    pairing with its own ENTER. PER-FRAME. So removing `this()` from spellLeaf
    ARMS KANT-8 exactly as SEQ 31 step 4 predicts -- the save/restore machinery
    really does run, and a returned LOCAL really will come back emptied.

    iterT1 already self-called by name and passed per-frame; this narrows the
    result to a plain scalar local and makes it explicit rather than inferred
    from a fixture that was measuring iterator cursors.

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    Q2. `.firsT` DOES NOT FILTER BY AFFILIATION -- so SEQ 31 step 3's
        `inner := argument.firsT;` IS WRONG ON AN OPT PLAN NODE.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    planTerm builds an OPT as (genParse.rtn:456):

        opt = new("OPT");   opt +% at;   opt += node;

    -- the `at` ATTRIBUTE first, the wrapped term as a MEMBER second.
    Attributes and members share ONE list distinguished by affiliation
    (termScratch finding 4). The iterator being replaced says `on argument
    MEMBERS`; `.firsT` is plain `firstInList` (Instruct.rtn:145).

    MEASURED on a deliberately-built same-shape node:

        GOT=          atx     <- .firsT
        FIRSTMEMBER=  kidx    <- iterate ... on shape members
        FIRSTANY=     atx     <- iterate ... on shape (unfiltered)

    `.firsT` == unfiltered iterate. On an OPT node it returns the `at`
    attribute, not the wrapped term. A member-filtered accessor is needed, or
    the descent stays an iterator.

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    BONUS DEFECT, PRE-EXISTING, SURFACED NOT CAUSED -- `.firsT`/`.lasT`
    SEGFAULT ON ANY LEAF NODE.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    NOT exercised by this fixture (it would crash the run); recorded here
    because it was found by the first cut, which descended via `.firsT` and
    died at 139 on the third level. Crash frame 0 is opDot, GroupRules.mm:4373.

    Instruct.rtn:145 reads as guarded:

        case 403:   if !target.firstInList  product = null;
                    else product = target.firstInList;

    but tok generates the guard as

        if ( !target->groupBody->groupList->firstInList )

    -- which dereferences `groupList` IN ORDER TO TEST IT. A node with no list
    has groupList == 0, so the guard segfaults on precisely the case it exists
    to handle. Cases 401/402 (`.nexT`/`.prioR`) are safe: they generate
    `!target->nextInParent`, a direct field with no intermediate pointer. Only
    403/404 (`.firsT`/`.lasT`) go through groupBody->groupList.

    Reproduce: any `x.firsT` where x carries no list. It is a null-guard that
    dereferences the pointer it is guarding, so it is not a tok bug -- the
    incant source says `target.firstInList` and the intermediate is implicit.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(FrameTest);
define
    deep;
    inner   deep;
    outer   inner;

    probe argument code={
        mark = #"L-" taG argument;
        print "  ENTER " mark:;
        iterate kid on *argument;
        if ++kid;
            probe(kid);
        print "  AFTER " mark:;
        };

    shapeProbe argument code={
        shape = new("shape");
        atx   = new("atx");
        shape +% atx;
        kidx  = new("kidx");
        shape += kidx;
        got  := shape.firsT;
        print "GOT=" got:;
        iterate m members on shape;
        if ++m;
            print "FIRSTMEMBER=" m:;
        iterate a on shape;
        if ++a;
            print "FIRSTANY=" a:;
        };

    fixProbe argument code={
        shape = new("shape");
        atx   = new("atx");
        shape +% atx;
        kidx  = new("kidx");
        shape += kidx;
        mem  := shape.firstMembeR;
        print "NEWFIRSTMEMBER=" mem:;
        leaf  = new("leaf");
        edge := leaf.firsT;
        print "LEAFFIRST-SURVIVED=" edge:;
        emt  := leaf.firstMembeR;
        print "LEAFFIRSTMEMBER-SURVIVED=" emt:;
        };
    ;

print "=== Q1  named self-call: per-frame or shared? ===":;
probe(outer);
print "=== Q2  .firsT affiliation on an attribute-then-member shape ===":;
shapeProbe(outer);
print "=== G2  the 403/404 guard fix and the new .firstMembeR ===":;
fixProbe(outer);

